error[E0277]: `std::io::Error` is not an `ApiError`, so a transparent variant cannot answer as it
  --> tests/ui/macros/api_error_transparent_not_an_api_error.rs:11:16
   |
11 |     Io(#[from] std::io::Error),
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not an `ApiError`
   |
   = help: the trait `IntoProblem` is not implemented for `std::io::Error`
   = note: a variant marked `#[error(transparent)]` or `#[problem(transparent)]` answers with the problem, statuses and responses of the error it holds; derive `kynos::ApiError` for `std::io::Error`
   = note: a variant whose message is its field's but whose failure is its own declares `#[problem(status = ...)]`, which makes it no longer transparent
   = help: the following other types implement trait `IntoProblem`:
             AtCapacity<T>
             AuthRejection
             BodyRefused<T, U>
             BodyRejection
             BodySizeExceeded<T>
             ConnectInfoRejection
             CookieRejection
             CrossSite<T>
           and $N others
   = note: required for `std::io::Error` to implement `kynos::__private::problem::HeldError`

